# Shared edge proxy — the single owner of :80 / :443 on the VPS.
#
# The box hosts two independent compose stacks (YuPay and streamers-parser).
# Only one process can bind the privileged ports, so neither stack's own Caddy
# does: this one accepts every inbound request, terminates TLS, and forwards
# cleartext HTTP to the stack that owns the hostname over the ``yupay-edge``
# docker network. Each stack keeps its own routing/CSP/auth rules in its own
# Caddyfile — this file only decides which stack a hostname belongs to.
#
# See ADR-0030 and docs/runbooks/deploy-shared-vps.md.

{
	# Let's Encrypt expiry warnings land here.
	email ops@yupay.uz
}

# ---------- YuPay ----------
# One block for all five hostnames: the upstream (the YuPay stack's Caddy)
# re-routes by Host, and Caddy forwards the original Host header untouched.
# Certificates are issued per-hostname via HTTP-01 on :80.
#
# Whatever the path in, exactly one X-Forwarded-For value reaches the stack: the
# real client. The API trusts the *first* entry of that chain (``_client_ip`` in
# bootstrap.py, which feeds the slowapi rate limiter, the auth IP guard and the
# Payme webhook allowlist in Caddyfile.prod), so an appended chain would let a
# caller pick whatever IP they like and spoof past all three.
#
# Where that value comes from depends on who the peer is, which is why the two
# handles below exist rather than one blanket rewrite:
#
#   * Direct client  — the peer IS the client, so {remote_host} is the truth and
#     any inbound X-Forwarded-For is attacker-controlled and must be discarded.
#   * Via Cloudflare — the peer is a Cloudflare edge, so {remote_host} would
#     replace the real client with a Cloudflare address: every visitor would
#     share a handful of IPs (breaking rate limiting) and genuine Payme calls
#     would fail the 185.234.113.0/28 allowlist with a 403. Cloudflare's own
#     CF-Connecting-IP carries the client, and it is trustworthy precisely
#     because the matcher below has already established the peer is Cloudflare.
#
# Both handles are always present, so the hostnames work whether their DNS
# records are proxied ("orange cloud") or DNS-only — flipping that switch needs
# no deploy, and a flip in either direction can't strand us.
#
# CF ranges are from https://www.cloudflare.com/ips-v4 + ips-v6 (fetched
# 2026-08-15). They change rarely; if Cloudflare adds a range, a client arriving
# over it simply falls through to the direct handle and is seen as its edge IP.
(yupay_upstream) {
	@cloudflare remote_ip 173.245.48.0/20 103.21.244.0/22 103.22.200.0/22 103.31.4.0/22 141.101.64.0/18 108.162.192.0/18 190.93.240.0/20 188.114.96.0/20 197.234.240.0/22 198.41.128.0/17 162.158.0.0/15 104.16.0.0/13 104.24.0.0/14 172.64.0.0/13 131.0.72.0/22 2400:cb00::/32 2606:4700::/32 2803:f800::/32 2405:b500::/32 2405:8100::/32 2a06:98c0::/29 2c0f:f248::/32

	handle @cloudflare {
		reverse_proxy yupay-caddy:80 {
			header_up X-Forwarded-For {http.request.header.Cf-Connecting-Ip}
		}
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy yupay-caddy:80 {
			header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}
		}
	}
}

yupay.uz, www.yupay.uz, app.yupay.uz, admin.yupay.uz, api.yupay.uz, grafana.yupay.uz {
	import yupay_upstream
}

# ---------- streamers-parser ----------
# Fronted by Cloudflare (proxied DNS). Cloudflare provides the public cert; the
# origin hop is secured with a self-signed cert (``tls internal``), which is
# what CF's "Full" mode expects. Declaring both schemes disables Caddy's
# HTTP→HTTPS redirect, which would otherwise loop under CF "Flexible".
# This mirrors what streamers-parser's own Caddy did before it moved behind
# this proxy — do not "fix" it into a Let's Encrypt block without checking the
# Cloudflare SSL mode first.
http://marketing.kolikosoft.com, https://marketing.kolikosoft.com {
	tls internal
	# No X-Forwarded-For rewrite here, unlike the YuPay block: the peer is
	# Cloudflare, not the end user, so overwriting the header would replace the
	# real client IP with a Cloudflare edge address. The inbound chain is the
	# trustworthy one.
	reverse_proxy streamers-caddy:80
}
